  "data_abstract": "The intense photon fluxes from relativistic nuclei provide an opportunity to study photonuclear interactions in ultraperipheral collisions. The measurement of coherently photoproduced \\fourpi~final states in ultraperipheral $\\rm{Pb\\textendash Pb}$ collisions at \\fivenn~is presented for the first time. The cross section, d$\\sigma$/d$y$, times the branching ratio ($\\rho\\rightarrow \\pi^+ \\pi^+ \\pi^- \\pi^-$) is found to be $47.8\\pm2.3~\\rm{\\rm{(stat.)}}\\pm7.7~\\rm{\\rm{(syst.)}}$~mb in the rapidity interval $|y| < 0.5$. The invariant mass distribution is best described by the fit assuming two excited resonances, $\\rho(1450)$ and $\\rho(1700)$, and the interference term between them. The values of the masses ($m$) and widths ($\\Gamma$) of the resonances extracted from the fit are $m_{1}=1385\\pm14~\\rm{(stat.)}\\pm3~\\rm{(syst.)}$~\\MeVmass, $\\Gamma_{1}=431\\pm36~\\rm{(stat.)}\\pm82~\\rm{(syst.)}$~\\MeVmass, $m_{2}=1663\\pm13~\\rm{(stat.)}\\pm22~\\rm{(syst.)}$~\\MeVmass~and $\\Gamma_{2}=357~\\pm31~\\rm{(stat.)}\\pm49~\\rm{(syst.)}$ \\MeVmass, respectively. The measured cross sections times the branching ratios are compared to recent theoretical predictions.",
